1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,940
Hello again!

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:04,340
Last time, we learned something clever.

3
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:08,440
When adding gets stuck, a friend can rescue us.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,220
Do you remember the trick?

5
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:15,820
We take away the friend, and then we add five.

6
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:19,720
Today the beads get stuck a different way.

7
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,720
This time, we are taking away.

8
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:26,920
The rule is still the same as last time.

9
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:30,080
Always look at the lower beads first.

10
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:33,280
If there are enough, just take them away.

11
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:37,800
Let us try nine take away two.

12
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:40,580
Make nine on your abacus.

13
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:43,520
Now take two lower beads away.

14
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:45,920
That was easy.

15
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,640
Nine take away two is seven.

16
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:51,680
No friend needed there at all.

17
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:56,140
Now let us try five take away one.

18
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,000
Make five on your abacus.

19
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:02,200
Look carefully at the lower beads.

20
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,120
How many lower beads do you have?

21
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:08,260
None at all.

22
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,480
The upper bead is holding all of the five.

23
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:14,140
So how can we take one away?

24
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:17,400
There is nothing down here to take.

25
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:20,400
Look at that, we are stuck.

26
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:24,000
Do not worry, we know what to do.

27
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,600
One's friend is four.

28
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:29,900
Last time, the friend helped us add.

29
00:01:30,580 --> 00:01:33,140
This time, the friend helps us take away.

30
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,520
Here is the trick.

31
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:39,040
First, we add the friend to the lower beads.

32
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:41,880
Then, we take away five.

33
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,840
Remember, lower beads move first.

34
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:48,620
So add four lower beads now.

35
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:51,800
The rod shows nine.

36
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,700
Now take away five.

37
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:57,240
Push the upper bead up.

38
00:01:58,360 --> 00:01:59,980
The rod shows four.

39
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:03,660
Five take away one is four.

40
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:07,720
We had nothing to take, and we still did it.

41
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:11,680
Let us try six take away two.

42
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,680
Make six on your abacus.

43
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,460
Look at the lower beads.

44
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:20,980
There is only one, and we need two.

45
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,500
So we call a friend.

46
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,080
Two's friend is three.

47
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:29,340
Add three lower beads first.

48
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,080
The rod shows nine.

49
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,960
Now take away five.

50
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:37,600
Push the upper bead up.

51
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,220
The rod shows four.

52
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:43,980
Six take away two is four.

53
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:48,180
You are doing so well with these tricky ones.

54
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:52,840
If you are enjoying this, please like the video and subscribe.

55
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:56,300
Now, let us try one more together.

56
00:02:57,480 --> 00:03:00,680
Let us try seven take away four.

57
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,640
Make seven on your abacus.

58
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,220
Look at the lower beads.

59
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:09,440
There are two, and we need four.

60
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:12,380
Four's friend is one.

61
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:15,500
Add one lower bead first.

62
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,960
The rod shows eight.

63
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:21,160
Now take away five.

64
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,620
Push the upper bead up.

65
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,620
The rod shows three.

66
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:30,580
Seven take away four is three.

67
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,000
Did you see the pattern?

68
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:38,040
It is the same trick as last time, just the other way round.

69
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:43,180
Last time, we took away the friend, and then added five.

70
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:48,260
This time, we add the friend, and then take away five.

71
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:52,260
Every time, we did the same two things.

72
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:54,160
Add the friend first.

73
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,320
Then take away five.

74
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:58,420
The friend changes.

75
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:00,740
The five never does.

76
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:05,180
Now it is your turn, all on your own.

77
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:07,900
Make six on your abacus.

78
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,300
Then take away three.

79
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:12,500
Think about it.

80
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:14,580
What is three's friend?

81
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:19,520
Add that friend to the lower beads first.

82
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:22,140
Then take away five.

83
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,940
What number is showing now?

84
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,720
Six take away three is three.

85
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:31,520
Did you get it right?

86
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:36,640
Well done, you used the trick all by yourself.

87
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:42,360
Now you know the small friends for taking away too.

88
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:45,140
Try them on your own abacus at home.

89
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:50,160
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

90
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,020
Download it free.

91
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:57,720
Next time, we will mix everything together in one big game.

92
00:04:58,540 --> 00:04:59,760
See you next time!
